<section id="home" class="hero section"><div class="hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">INFORMATION SYSTEMS • TECHNICAL SUPPORT • OPERATIONS</p><h1>Kyle Lyndon<br><span>N. Surla</span></h1><p class="role-line"><span class="status-dot"></span> Adaptable professional focused on technology, support, operations & practical solutions.</p><p class="lead">Information Systems graduate with hands-on experience in application support, IT operations, technical troubleshooting, QA testing, system administration, and user support — ready to contribute across technical, support, operations, and other professional environments.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn primary" href="#contact">Contact Me</a><a class="btn ghost" href="#experience">View Experience</a><a class="btn ghost resume-btn" href="assets/Kyle_Lyndon_Surla_Resume.pdf" download>Download Resume <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div><div class="quick"><span>Metro Manila, Philippines</span><span>Open to diverse opportunities</span><span>BS Information Systems</span></div></div><button class="portrait-wrap image-trigger" type="button" data-image="assets/profile.png" data-caption="Kyle Lyndon N. Surla — Professional Portrait" aria-label="Professional portrait"><div class="glow"></div><img src="assets/profile.png" alt="Professional portrait of Kyle Lyndon N. Surla"></button></section>
<section id="about" class="section"><p class="eyebrow">ABOUT ME</p><h2>Technology, support,<br>and adaptable problem-solving.</h2><div class="impact-strip"><div><strong>2</strong><span>IT support roles</span></div><div><strong>BSIS</strong><span>Information Systems</span></div><div><strong>QA</strong><span>Testing & validation</span></div><div><strong>USER</strong><span>Focused support</span></div></div><div class="about-grid"><p>I’m an Information Systems graduate with hands-on experience in Application Support, IT Operations, technical troubleshooting, system administration, and user support. I have supported business applications, performed QA testing and system installations, resolved technical issues, assisted users, and documented system incidents and solutions.</p><p>I enjoy learning how systems work behind the scenes and finding practical solutions to technical concerns. I’m continuously expanding my skills in IT support, databases, web technologies, system development, communication, and operations. I’m open to opportunities where my technical background, adaptability, analytical thinking, and support experience can add value.</p></div></section>
<section id="experience" class="section"><p class="eyebrow">EXPERIENCE</p><h2>Professional experience</h2><div class="timeline"><article class="detail-card" tabindex="0" role="button" data-title="Application Support — Executive Optical (EO)" data-detail="Supported business applications and branch users through technical troubleshooting, system installation, QA testing, application monitoring, software updates, and clear issue documentation. This role strengthened my ability to analyze incidents, communicate with users, validate fixes, and keep day-to-day systems reliable."><div class="date">AUG 2025 — SEP 27, 2026</div><div><h3>Application Support</h3><h4>Executive Optical (EO)</h4><p>Provided technical support and troubleshooting for business applications and systems, performed basic installation and QA testing, assisted users with system concerns, monitored application performance, supported updates, and documented issues and resolutions.</p></div></article><article class="detail-card" tabindex="0" role="button" data-title="IT Specialist — Tutoring KR" data-detail="Provided technical support for devices, applications, and systems. Responsibilities included troubleshooting, system updates, security support, user account management, daily IT operations, and assistance with system enhancements in a fast-paced environment."><div class="date">NOV 2023 — OCT 2024</div><div><h3>IT Specialist</h3><h4>Tutoring KR</h4><p>Provided technical support for devices, applications, and systems. Managed system updates, security, and user accounts while assisting daily IT operations and system enhancements.</p></div></article></div></section>
<section id="skills" class="section"><p class="eyebrow">TECHNICAL SKILLS</p><h2>Tools I use to keep<br>technology working.</h2><div class="cards"><article class="detail-card" tabindex="0" role="button" data-title="IT Support" data-detail="Hands-on support experience covering hardware and software troubleshooting, user assistance, system support, maintenance, and documenting technical concerns and resolutions."><b>01</b><h3>IT Support</h3><p>Hardware & software troubleshooting<br>System support & maintenance<br>Documentation & reporting</p></article><article class="detail-card" tabindex="0" role="button" data-title="Systems Support" data-detail="Experience assisting with system installation, QA testing, software updates, recovery and backup tasks, and basic network configuration as part of day-to-day technical support."><b>02</b><h3>Systems</h3><p>Installation & QA testing<br>Updates, recovery & backup<br>Basic network configuration</p></article><article class="detail-card" tabindex="0" role="button" data-title="Support Tools" data-detail="Comfortable working with Windows, Microsoft Office, Google Workspace, AnyDesk, and TeamViewer for productivity, collaboration, user support, and remote troubleshooting."><b>03</b><h3>Tools</h3><p>Windows • Microsoft Office<br>Google Workspace<br>AnyDesk • TeamViewer</p></article><article class="detail-card" tabindex="0" role="button" data-title="Web & Problem Solving" data-detail="Uses HTML fundamentals, browser and email management, critical thinking, and logical troubleshooting to understand technical issues and identify practical solutions."><b>04</b><h3>Web & Problem Solving</h3><p>HTML basics<br>Browser & email management<br>Logical & analytical troubleshooting</p></article></div></section>
<section class="section approach"><p class="eyebrow">HOW I WORK</p><h2>A practical support mindset.</h2><div class="approach-grid"><article class="detail-card" tabindex="0" role="button" data-title="Understand" data-detail="I begin by clarifying the issue, symptoms, user impact, and environment. Good troubleshooting starts with a clear understanding of what changed and what the user expects."><span>01</span><h3>Understand</h3><p>Clarify the issue, user impact, symptoms, and environment before changing anything.</p></article><article class="detail-card" tabindex="0" role="button" data-title="Troubleshoot" data-detail="I isolate likely causes and test logically, starting with safe and reversible checks before applying a solution."><span>02</span><h3>Troubleshoot</h3><p>Isolate likely causes, test logically, and use the safest effective solution.</p></article><article class="detail-card" tabindex="0" role="button" data-title="Validate" data-detail="After a fix, I confirm expected behavior and check whether the original issue is fully resolved rather than assuming success."><span>03</span><h3>Validate</h3><p>Confirm the fix, check expected behavior, and reduce the chance of repeat incidents.</p></article><article class="detail-card" tabindex="0" role="button" data-title="Document" data-detail="I record the issue, troubleshooting steps, and resolution so future support can be faster, clearer, and more consistent."><span>04</span><h3>Document</h3><p>Record the issue and resolution so future support becomes faster and more consistent.</p></article></div></section><section id="education" class="section"><p class="eyebrow">EDUCATION</p><h2>Education</h2><div class="edu"><article class="detail-card" tabindex="0" role="button" data-title="Bachelor of Science in Information Systems" data-detail="University of Caloocan City • 2019–2023. My degree built a foundation in information systems, technology, business processes, databases, and problem solving that supports my practical IT experience."><span>2019 — 2023</span><h3>University of Caloocan City</h3><p>Bachelor of Science in Information Systems</p></article><article class="detail-card" tabindex="0" role="button" data-title="Accountancy Business Management" data-detail="APEC Schools – North Fairview • 2017–2019. Senior high school studies in Accountancy Business Management provided additional exposure to business processes, communication, and organizational fundamentals."><span>2017 — 2019</span><h3>APEC Schools – North Fairview</h3><p>Accountancy Business Management</p></article></div></section>
<section id="contact" class="section contact"><p class="eyebrow">LET'S CONNECT</p><h2>Let’s build something<br>valuable together.</h2><p>I’m open to diverse professional opportunities where I can contribute my technical knowledge, support experience, communication, adaptability, and problem-solving skills while continuing to learn and grow.</p><div class="availability"><span class="status-dot"></span><strong>Available for opportunities</strong> <span>• Metro Manila, Philippines</span></div><div class="actions"><a class="btn primary" href="mailto:kylelyndonsurla@gmail.com">Email Me</a><a class="btn ghost" href="tel:+639397257753">Call Me</a><a class="btn ghost resume-btn" href="assets/Kyle_Lyndon_Surla_Resume.pdf" download>Download Resume <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div><div class="contact-info"><a href="mailto:kylelyndonsurla@gmail.com">kylelyndonsurla@gmail.com</a><span>0939 725 7753</span></div></section>
